dcterms:license a owl:AnnotationProperty .

swrla:isRuleEnabled a owl:AnnotationProperty .

owl:Thing rdfs:comment """A 'thing' represents the Livestock Farming Theft Detection Ontology(LFTDO).
The purpose of Livestock Farming Theft Detection Ontology(LFTDO) is to integrate and analyze data from various sources, such as sensor networks, surveillance cameras, and databases, to identify suspicious activities that may indicate theft in a farming area. Furthermore, it enables livestock theft detection and prevention systems and applications to be accessible, flexible, transparent, interoperable, scalable, and cost effective.  
The aim is to assist with the early detection of livestock theft by providing a structured and standardized way of representing knowledge about livestock farming, including: 
1.Types of livestock

2.The vital components of livestock farming include ownership, farming areas, grazing areas, water sources, and technological resources (i.e. IoT devices, gateways, cloud computing, and machine-learning algorithms).

3.A variety of activities happening such as livestock movement, grazing, and feeding.

4.The people involved in livestock farming include farmers, extended-farmer officers, law enforcement agencies, and veterinarians.

5.A variety of events occurs in a farming area such as livestock theft   
LFTDO standardizes the data structures, integration, and knowledge representation of livestock farming by defining the concepts, entities, relationships, and rules governing them. 

The ontology should be able to reason livestock behaviour patterns and environmental conditions data provided to infer the possibility of livestock theft to alert livestock farmers and other stakeholders.

Main Entities:
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.Actor
2.Behaviour
3.BehaviourState
4.CloudService
5.Device
6.EnvironmentaCondition
7.Livestock
8.Locatio
9.HealthCondition""" .

<https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO> a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:license "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" ;
    rdfs:comment """Livestock Farming Theft Detection Ontology(LFTDO)
Author: Tumelo Modise, 209332175,Date : 13 September 2023,
Updated: 01/03/2026
University: Tshwane University of Technology(TUT)
Subject:Masters of Computing in Computer Science 
Supervisors: Dr A Buitengdag,Dr Z Dawood,Prof J

Introduction
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Livestock Farming Theft Detection Ontology(LFTDO) is a formal Livestock Farming ontology. The focus of the ontology will be on the agriculture domain for Livestock Theft Detection concepts.
The purpose of constructing this ontology is to provide a cognitive knowledge-based model for the Livestock Farming domain to be used by the farmers and veterinaries with a goal of Improving Livestock Farming Management to reduce livestock theft, and reducing cost. The ontology should be able to reason on the Livestock Behaviours to detect the abnormally provided by the devices fitted on the livestock with sensor  to infer potential theft to farmer.

Purpose
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The purpose of Livestock Farming Theft Detection Ontology(LFTDO) is to integrate and analyze data from various sources, such as sensor networks, surveillance cameras, and databases, to identify suspicious activities that may indicate theft in a farming area. Furthermore, it enables livestock theft detection and prevention systems and applications to be accessible, flexible, transparent, interoperable, scalable, and cost effective.  
The aim is to assist with the early detection of livestock theft by providing a structured and standardized way of representing knowledge about livestock farming, including: 
1.Types of livestock
2.The vital components of livestock farming include ownership, farming areas, grazing areas, water sources, and technological resources (i.e. IoT devices, gateways, cloud computing, and machine-learning algorithms).
3.A variety of activities happening such as livestock movement, grazing, and feeding,
4.The people involved in livestock farming include farmers, extended-farmer officers, law enforcement agencies, and veterinarians.
5.A variety of events occurs in a farming area such as livestock theft   
LFTDO standardizes the data structures, integration, and knowledge representation of livestock farming by defining the concepts, entities, relationships, and rules governing them. The ontology should be able to reason livestock behaviour patterns and environmental conditions data provided to infer the possibility of livestock theft to alert livestock farmers and other stakeholders."""^^xsd:string ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO/v0.12> ;
    owl:versionInfo 12 .

LFTDO4:AbnormalBodyTemperature a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "AbnormalBodyTemperature" ;
    rdfs:comment "The Abnormal body temperature is the opposite of any normal defined body temperature for Livestock." ;
    rdfs:subClassOf LFTDO4:BodyTemperature ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( LFTDO4:BodyTemperature [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty LFTDO4:healthConditionBelongsTo ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom LFTDO4:Livestock ] ) ] .

LFTDO4:Algorithm002 a owl:NamedIndividual,
        LFTDO4:Algorithm ;
    rdfs:label "Algorithm002" ;
    rdfs:comment "Algorithm002" ;
    LFTDO4:hasAlgorithmType "Moving Average"^^xsd:string ;
    LFTDO4:hasAlgorithmVersion "v0.1"^^xsd:string ;
    LFTDO4:hasComplexity "HIGH"^^xsd:string ;
    LFTDO4:hasDetectionMethodAccuracy 0.98 ;
    LFTDO4:isOptimized false ;
    LFTDO4:isUsedBy LFTDO4:GPSTrackingMethod .

LFTDO4:AudioMonitoringSystem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "AudioMonitoringSystem" ;
    rdfs:comment "AudioMonitoringSystem is a theft DetectionMethod" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasDetectionMethodAccuracy ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:analyses ;
            owl:someValuesFrom LFTDO4:Database ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:uses ;
            owl:someValuesFrom LFTDO4:Algorithm ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasMethodAttribute ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasFalsePositiveRate ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasDetectionMethodType ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasTrainingData ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:boolean ],
        LFTDO4:DetectionMethod .

LFTDO4:BehaviorMonitoringSystem a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "BehaviourMonitoringSystem" ;
    rdfs:comment "BehaviourMonitoringSystem is a theft DetectionMethod" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasDetectionMethodType ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:analyses ;
            owl:someValuesFrom LFTDO4:Database ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasDetectionMethodAccuracy ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasFalsePositiveRate ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasMethodAttribute ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:string ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasTrainingData ;
            owl:someValuesFrom xsd:boolean ],
        [ a owl:Restriction ;
            owl:onProperty LFTDO4:uses ;
            owl:someValuesFrom LFTDO4:Algorithm ],
        LFTDO4:DetectionMethod .

LFTDO4:CattleRestingState a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment "CattleRestingState is a NormalState" ;
    rdfs:subClassOf LFTDO4:NormalState .

LFTDO4:CattleWithFever a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CattleWithFever" ;
    rdfs:comment "Cattle that hasBodyTemperature >= 39.4 celsius, is a Cattle with Fever" ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( LFTDO4:Cattle [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty LFTDO4:experiences ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom LFTDO4:Fever ] [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasBodyTemperature ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom [ a rdfs:Datatype ;
                                owl:onDatatype xsd:decimal ;
                                owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minExclusive 39.3 ] ) ] ] ) ] .

LFTDO4:CattleWithHighAbnormalBodyTempareture a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CattleWithHighAbnormalBodyTempareture" ;
    rdfs:comment """Check the transition from normal to abnormal livestock Health condition when, for instance, a Cow's Body temperature
deviates from an normal body temperature of a healthy adult cow, which ranges from 38°C to 39.3°C, with an average of approximately 38.6°C.The the exceeded deviation from the norm could indicate synificant anomly and resulting in a potential theft or health alert issued to the farmer. 

e.g. Cattle with an Abnormal Body Temperatute has a hasBodyTemperature outside the normal range [>=38,>39.3]""" ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( LFTDO4:Cattle [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasBodyTemperature ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom [ a rdfs:Datatype ;
                                owl:onDatatype xsd:decimal ;
                                owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minExclusive 39.3 ] ) ] ] ) ] .

LFTDO4:CattleWithLowAbnormalBodyTempareture a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "CattleWithLowAbnormalBodyTempareture" ;
    rdfs:comment """Check the transition from normal to abnormal livestock Health condition when, for instance, a Cow's Body temperature
deviates from an normal body temperature of a healthy adult cow, which ranges from 38°C to 39.3°C, with an average of approximately 38.6°C.The the exceeded deviation from the norm could indicate synificant anomly and resulting in a potential theft or health alert issued to the farmer. 

e.g. Cattle with an Abnormal Body Temperatute has a hasBodyTemperature outside the normal range [>=38,>39.3]""" ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( LFTDO4:Cattle [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasBodyTemperature ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom [ a rdfs:Datatype ;
                                owl:onDatatype xsd:decimal ;
                                owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:maxExclusive 38.0 ] ) ] ] ) ] .

LFTDO4:CattleWithNormalBodyTempareture a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:comment """Check the transition from normal to abnormal livestock Health condition when, for instance, a Cow's Body temperature
deviates from an normal body temperature of a healthy adult cow, which ranges from 38°C to 39.3°C, with an average of approximately 38.6°C.The the exceeded deviation from the norm could indicate synificant anomly and resulting in a potential theft or health alert issued to the farmer. 

e.g. Cattle with an Abnormal Body Temperatute has a hasBodyTemperature outside the normal range [>=38,>39.3]""" ;
    owl:equivalentClass [ a owl:Class ;
            owl:intersectionOf ( LFTDO4:Cattle [ a owl:Restriction ;
                        owl:onProperty LFTDO4:hasBodyTemperature ;
                        owl:someValuesFrom [ a rdfs:Datatype ;
                                owl:onDatatype xsd:decimal ;
                                owl:withRestrictions ( [ xsd:minInclusive 38.0 ] [ xsd:maxInclusive 39.3 ] ) ] ] ) ] .

